WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.360
Last question today is from Nico.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:07.650
Nico wrote in and said, Hey David, what's
the most unrealistic democratic campaign promise

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:08.920
of 2020 so far?

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.200
Obviously Donald Trump all along was making
unrealistic campaign promises, but what are

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.530
unrealistic ones from the left?

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.369
So there's two ways to answer this question.

00:00:17.369 --> 00:00:20.130
There's the micro answer and there's the macro
answer.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:25.249
If you want to play the micro of specific
policy, there are lots of policies that are

00:00:25.249 --> 00:00:30.670
unrealistic in the sense that they ignore
that you would need as president, both the

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:36.100
House and Senate to be democratically controlled
in order to make them a reality almost guaranteed.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:40.859
Okay, so medicare for all for example, how
do you do Medicare for all without control

00:00:40.859 --> 00:00:46.519
of the Senate in 2020 yes, it's possible in
the hypothetical sense, it's extraordinarily

00:00:46.519 --> 00:00:47.530
unlikely.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:53.379
There's certain infrastructure stuff that's
not realistic in terms of its political viability

00:00:53.379 --> 00:00:57.960
without control of the House and Senate and
you have to understand that we have many examples

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:03.180
even with control by the same party of the
White House, the house in the Senate, it's

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.710
still hard to do stuff.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:05.890
Universal background checks.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:10.730
When Barack Obama was in the White House and
controlled the House and Senate, 90% support

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.690
for that from the American public.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:13.800
Still couldn't get it done.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.890
Gun lobby significantly to blame there.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:21.190
But the point is there are lots of policies
that are effectively nonstarters if you don't

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:24.570
control the White House, the Senate and the
House of Representatives.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:25.570
But that's the micro.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:29.470
I think this question is more interestingly
addressed at the macro level.

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:35.020
The most unrealistic metta or macro promise
is bipartisanship.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.880
Everybody pays lip service to bipartisanship.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.950
I know how to work with the other side.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:44.750
I have a long history of drafting and sponsoring
legislation with people from the other side

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:45.750
of the aisle.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.310
I would work together in ways that other candidates
aren't able to.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:50.610
I don't think it's a bad idea.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.310
It's just completely unrealistic.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:56.590
The last 30 years have increased polarization
have shown us this.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:01.160
I did a story on the Monday show talking about
how Donald Trump is in practice.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:07.620
Just a symptom of the problem, which has been
the rise in reactionary politics from the

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.220
right for the last 20 to 30 years.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:12.690
Depending on how you want to measure it.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:16.930
Republicans won't even call out Trump for
relatively minor things.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:19.940
You're not going to get real bipartisanship
in this environment.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:25.960
There's no upside to even trying to get bipartisanship
the way our political system is designed and

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:31.480
you actually risk your own party turning against
you, uh, if you start working with the other

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:32.480
side.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.850
So I'm not saying I don't want bipartisanship.

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:41.000
I'm not saying that the people promising it
are straight up lying or don't want it themselves.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.080
What I'm telling you is that if you ask me
what's the most unrealistic promise we hear

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:49.730
from Democratic candidates is that they are
going to be able to work with Republicans

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:55.020
if they are elected Republicans who likely
will control the Senate after 2020 and get

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.060
stuff done.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.360
They will have to get stuff done despite Republicans.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.260
I would love to hear them just say that, and
that's the most unrealistic promise that we're

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.260
hearing.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:04.820
Um, that's it for today.

